---
/**
 * The /webmcp headline (docs/projects/redesign/design-export-remaining/design_handoff_webmcp,
 * band 1).
 *
 * The right block is the page's "same tools, as data" rail: the two JSON endpoints the catalog
 * below is generated from. They are the only links in the hero, and they are the same two rows
 * band 6 opens with — stated twice on purpose, because an agent reading the top of the page
 * should not have to reach the bottom to find the manifest.
 *
 * THE HERO'S TYPE AND LAYOUT ARE `.rd-hero` IN global.css: the H1, the 32ch lede, the row, the
 * right block's hairline shell and the 720px collapse. The rail sat in a 320px grid column beside
 * the lede until 2026-09-05, with its own 900px stack and a left-rule-to-top-rule swap; it now
 * sits on the shell's right edge, where every page's right block sits.
 */
---

{/*
  A div, not a section — the same call every other redesigned hero made: `npm run validate:html`
  names an h1 inside sectioning content, and an unnamed <section> is not exposed as a region.

  `data-module` is retro.css's hook, per the hero/body split every other converted surface uses:
  retro restyles this markup rather than being handed a hero of its own.
*/}
<div class="rd-section rd-hero webmcp-hero" data-module="webmcp-hero">
  <h1><span class="rd-fill">WebMCP</span></h1>

  <div class="hero-row">
    <p class="hero-statement">
      Six typed tools this page hands to an agent, and what they return.
    </p>
    <div class="hero-aside hero-data">
      <span class="hero-data-label">The same tools, as data</span>
      <a class="hero-data-link" href="/webmcp/tools.json">webmcp/tools.json</a>
      <a class="hero-data-link" href="/webmcp/index.json">webmcp/index.json</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<style>
  .webmcp-hero { padding-top: 72px; }

  .hero-data { gap: 6px; }

  .hero-data-label {
    margin-bottom: 4px;
    font-size: 18px;
    color: var(--ink-6);
  }

  .hero-data-link {
    font-family: var(--font-mono-plex);
    font-size: 20px;
    color: var(--agents);
  }

  .hero-data-link:hover { color: var(--agents-hover); }

  @media (max-width: 720px) {
    .webmcp-hero { padding-top: 52px; }

    /* 44px tap target on every small in-content link, per the mobile spec. */
    .hero-data-link {
      display: inline-flex;
      align-items: center;
      min-height: 44px;
    }
  }
</style>
